<h1 data-start=3D"461" data-end=3D"483" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"46=
3" data-end=3D"483">1. Encapsulation</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"484" data-end=3D"505" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"48=
7" data-end=3D"505">1.1 D=C3=A9finition</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"506" data-end=3D"797" class=3D"">L'<strong data-start=3D"5=
08" data-end=3D"525">encapsulation</strong> est le m=C3=A9canisme qui consi=
ste =C3=A0 <strong data-start=3D"558" data-end=3D"589">cacher les d=C3=A9ta=
ils internes</strong> d'une classe et =C3=A0 contr=C3=B4ler l'acc=C3=A8s =
=C3=A0 ses donn=C3=A9es. En Java, cela est r=C3=A9alis=C3=A9 en <strong dat=
a-start=3D"670" data-end=3D"721">restreignant l'acc=C3=A8s aux attributs d'=
une classe</strong> et en fournissant des <strong data-start=3D"744" data-e=
nd=3D"775">m=C3=A9thodes d'acc=C3=A8s contr=C3=B4l=C3=A9es</strong> (getter=
s et setters).</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"799" data-end=3D"846" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"80=
3" data-end=3D"846">1.2 Pourquoi utiliser l'encapsulation ?</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"847" data-end=3D"1125">
<li data-start=3D"847" data-end=3D"939" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"849" data-end=3D"939" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"849=
" data-end=3D"873">S=C3=A9curit=C3=A9 des donn=C3=A9es</strong> : Emp=C3=AA=
che l'acc=C3=A8s ou la modification des attributs sans contr=C3=B4le.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"940" data-end=3D"1051" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"942" data-end=3D"1051" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"94=
2" data-end=3D"956">Modularit=C3=A9</strong> : Permet de modifier la mise e=
n =C5=93uvre interne sans impacter les classes qui utilisent l=E2=80=99obje=
t.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1052" data-end=3D"1125" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1054" data-end=3D"1125" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
054" data-end=3D"1081">Facilit=C3=A9 de maintenance</strong> : R=C3=A9duit =
les d=C3=A9pendances entre les classes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1127" data-end=3D"1161" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1131" data-end=3D"1161">1.3 Impl=C3=A9mentation en Java</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1162" data-end=3D"1236" class=3D"">En Java, l'encapsulatio=
n est r=C3=A9alis=C3=A9e avec des <strong data-start=3D"1209" data-end=3D"1=
234">modificateurs d=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1237" data-end=3D"1458">
<li data-start=3D"1237" data-end=3D"1293" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1239" data-end=3D"1293" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"123=
9" data-end=3D"1248">private</code> : Accessible uniquement dans la m=C3=AA=
me classe.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1294" data-end=3D"1329" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1296" data-end=3D"1329" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"129=
6" data-end=3D"1304">public</code> : Accessible de partout.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1330" data-end=3D"1401" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1332" data-end=3D"1401" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"133=
2" data-end=3D"1343">protected</code> : Accessible dans la m=C3=AAme classe=
 et par les sous-classes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1402" data-end=3D"1458" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1404" data-end=3D"1458" class=3D"">(sans modificateur) : A=
ccessible dans le m=C3=AAme package.</p>
</li>
</ul>
