<p data-start=3D"104" data-end=3D"410" class=3D"">Java est un langage orien=
t=C3=A9 objet, ce qui signifie que la programmation repose principalement s=
ur la manipulation d'<strong data-start=3D"220" data-end=3D"230">objets</st=
rong>. Un objet est une <strong data-start=3D"249" data-end=3D"274">instanc=
e d=E2=80=99une classe</strong>, et une <strong data-start=3D"283" data-end=
=3D"293">classe</strong> est un mod=C3=A8le ou un plan permettant de cr=C3=
=A9er des objets ayant des caract=C3=A9ristiques et des comportements sp=C3=
=A9cifiques.</p>
<p data-start=3D"412" data-end=3D"464" class=3D"">Dans ce tutoriel, nous al=
lons explorer en d=C3=A9tail :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"465" data-end=3D"665">
<li data-start=3D"465" data-end=3D"503" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"468" data-end=3D"503" class=3D"">La cr=C3=A9ation d=E2=80=
=99une classe en Java.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"504" data-end=3D"534" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"507" data-end=3D"534" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99instanciation d=
=E2=80=99objets.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"535" data-end=3D"572" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"538" data-end=3D"572" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99utilisation des=
 constructeurs.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"573" data-end=3D"606" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"576" data-end=3D"606" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99encapsulation d=
es donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"607" data-end=3D"665" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"610" data-end=3D"665" class=3D"">Les bonnes pratiques en p=
rogrammation orient=C3=A9e objet.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"667" data-end=3D"670" class=3D"">
