<h2 data-start=3D"5169" data-end=3D"5201" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5172" data-end=3D"5199">3. Destructeurs en Java</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"5202" data-end=3D"5349" class=3D"">Contrairement =C3=A0 C+=
+, <strong data-start=3D"5223" data-end=3D"5273">Java ne poss=C3=A8de pas d=
e destructeurs explicites</strong> car la m=C3=A9moire est g=C3=A9r=C3=A9e =
automatiquement par le <strong data-start=3D"5322" data-end=3D"5348">Garbag=
e Collector (GC)</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"5351" data-end=3D"5407" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5355" data-end=3D"5405">3.1 Gestion de la m=C3=A9moire et Garbage Collector=
</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5408" data-end=3D"5546">
<li data-start=3D"5408" data-end=3D"5480" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5410" data-end=3D"5480" class=3D"">Java lib=C3=A8re automa=
tiquement la m=C3=A9moire des objets <strong data-start=3D"5460" data-end=
=3D"5477">inaccessibles</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5481" data-end=3D"5546" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5483" data-end=3D"5546" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"5486" data-end=3D"5512">Garbage Collector (GC)</strong> d=C3=A9tecte et=
 supprime ces objets.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5548" data-end=3D"5582" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5552" data-end=3D"5580">3.2 M=C3=A9thode <code data-start=3D"5566" data-end=
=3D"5578">finalize()</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5583" data-end=3D"5674" class=3D"">Java propose la m=C3=A9=
thode <code data-start=3D"5607" data-end=3D"5619">finalize()</code>, ex=C3=
=A9cut=C3=A9e avant la destruction d=E2=80=99un objet par le GC.</p>
<p data-start=3D"5676" data-end=3D"5780" class=3D"">=E2=9A=A0 <strong data-=
start=3D"5678" data-end=3D"5691">Attention</strong> : <code data-start=3D"5=
694" data-end=3D"5706">finalize()</code> <strong data-start=3D"5707" data-e=
nd=3D"5723">est obsol=C3=A8te</strong> depuis Java 9 et son ex=C3=A9cution =
<strong data-start=3D"5755" data-end=3D"5777">n'est pas garantie</strong>.<=
/p>
