<h2 data-start=3D"6204" data-end=3D"6283" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6207" data-end=3D"6283">4. Quand Utiliser une Interface et Quand Utiliser u=
ne Classe Abstraite ?</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"6285" data-end=3D"6323" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6289" data-end=3D"6323">Utiliser une interface quand :</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6324" data-end=3D"6594">
<li data-start=3D"6324" data-end=3D"6380" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6326" data-end=3D"6380" class=3D"">Vous souhaitez d=C3=A9f=
inir un contrat sans impl=C3=A9mentation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6381" data-end=3D"6476" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6383" data-end=3D"6476" class=3D"">Vous avez besoin de <st=
rong data-start=3D"6403" data-end=3D"6424">multiple h=C3=A9ritage</strong> =
(une classe peut impl=C3=A9menter plusieurs interfaces).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6477" data-end=3D"6594" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6479" data-end=3D"6594" class=3D"">Vous voulez garantir qu=
e toutes les classes qui impl=C3=A9mentent l'interface respectent le m=C3=
=AAme contrat (m=C3=AAme m=C3=A9thode).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6596" data-end=3D"6641" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6600" data-end=3D"6641">Utiliser une classe abstraite quand :</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6642" data-end=3D"6946">
<li data-start=3D"6642" data-end=3D"6693" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6644" data-end=3D"6693" class=3D"">Vous avez une <strong d=
ata-start=3D"6658" data-end=3D"6692">hi=C3=A9rarchie de classes partag=C3=
=A9e</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6694" data-end=3D"6818" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6696" data-end=3D"6818" class=3D"">Vous voulez fournir une=
 <strong data-start=3D"6720" data-end=3D"6746">impl=C3=A9mentation de base<=
/strong> que certaines classes peuvent r=C3=A9utiliser et d'autres peuvent =
red=C3=A9finir.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6819" data-end=3D"6946" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6821" data-end=3D"6946" class=3D"">Vous avez des m=C3=A9th=
odes qui peuvent avoir une <strong data-start=3D"6866" data-end=3D"6894">im=
pl=C3=A9mentation partielle</strong> mais doivent =C3=AAtre compl=C3=A9t=C3=
=A9es dans les sous-classes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6948" data-end=3D"6951" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6953" data-end=3D"6973" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6956" data-end=3D"6973">5. Conclusion</strong></h2>
<ul data-start=3D"6975" data-end=3D"7311">
<li data-start=3D"6975" data-end=3D"7137" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6977" data-end=3D"7137" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
977" data-end=3D"6991">Interfaces</strong> : Permettent de d=C3=A9finir des=
 contrats stricts que les classes doivent respecter, elles favorisent le <s=
trong data-start=3D"7092" data-end=3D"7109">polymorphisme</strong> et l'<st=
rong data-start=3D"7115" data-end=3D"7136">h=C3=A9ritage multiple</strong>.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7138" data-end=3D"7311" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7140" data-end=3D"7311" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
140" data-end=3D"7162">Classes abstraites</strong> : Permettent de fournir =
une <strong data-start=3D"7191" data-end=3D"7219">impl=C3=A9mentation parti=
elle</strong> et offrent une meilleure <strong data-start=3D"7245" data-end=
=3D"7270">r=C3=A9utilisation du code</strong> pour les classes ayant une ba=
se commune.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"7313" data-end=3D"7536" class=3D"">L'utilisation appropri=
=C3=A9e des interfaces et des classes abstraites permet d=E2=80=99am=C3=A9l=
iorer la <strong data-start=3D"7401" data-end=3D"7416">flexibilit=C3=A9</st=
rong> et la <strong data-start=3D"7423" data-end=3D"7441">maintenabilit=C3=
=A9</strong> du code Java en exploitant pleinement les capacit=C3=A9s de l=
=E2=80=99<strong data-start=3D"7499" data-end=3D"7511">h=C3=A9ritage</stron=
g> et du <strong data-start=3D"7518" data-end=3D"7535">polymorphisme</stron=
g>.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article c=
