<ul data-start=3D"8148" data-end=3D"8383">
<li data-start=3D"8148" data-end=3D"8268" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8150" data-end=3D"8268" class=3D"">Nous soumettons trois t=
=C3=A2ches diff=C3=A9rentes au pool de threads et r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9rons leur=
s r=C3=A9sultats en utilisant <code data-start=3D"8253" data-end=3D"8267">f=
uture.get()</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8269" data-end=3D"8383" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8271" data-end=3D"8383" class=3D"">Les t=C3=A2ches s'ex=C3=
=A9cutent de mani=C3=A8re parall=C3=A8le, et nous attendons leur r=C3=A9sul=
tat dans l'ordre o=C3=B9 elles se terminent.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"8385" data-end=3D"8438" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
8389" data-end=3D"8438">3.2 Utilisation de <code data-start=3D"8410" data-e=
nd=3D"8421">invokeAll</code> et <code data-start=3D"8425" data-end=3D"8436"=
>invokeAny</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"8440" data-end=3D"8528" class=3D"">L'interface <code data-=
start=3D"8452" data-end=3D"8469">ExecutorService</code> fournit deux autres=
 m=C3=A9thodes pour g=C3=A9rer plusieurs t=C3=A2ches :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"8530" data-end=3D"8764">
