<p data-start=3D"2519" data-end=3D"2536" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
519" data-end=3D"2536">Explication :</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"2537" data-end=3D"2957">
<li data-start=3D"2537" data-end=3D"2649" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2539" data-end=3D"2649" class=3D"">Les deux threads <code =
data-start=3D"2556" data-end=3D"2565">thread1</code> et <code data-start=3D=
"2569" data-end=3D"2578">thread2</code> ex=C3=A9cutent la m=C3=A9thode <cod=
e data-start=3D"2600" data-end=3D"2613">increment()</code>, qui modifie la =
variable <code data-start=3D"2639" data-end=3D"2648">counter</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2650" data-end=3D"2828" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2652" data-end=3D"2828" class=3D"">Cependant, la ligne <co=
de data-start=3D"2672" data-end=3D"2683">counter++</code> n'est pas une op=
=C3=A9ration atomique. Cela signifie qu'il peut y avoir un conflit d'acc=C3=
=A8s entre les threads, ce qui entra=C3=AEne une <strong data-start=3D"2809=
" data-end=3D"2827">race condition</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2829" data-end=3D"2957" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2831" data-end=3D"2957" class=3D"">Le r=C3=A9sultat final =
de <code data-start=3D"2852" data-end=3D"2861">counter</code> pourrait =C3=
=AAtre inf=C3=A9rieur =C3=A0 2000, alors que nous nous attendions =C3=A0 ce=
 qu'il soit exactement 2000.</p>
</li>
</ul>
