<p data-start=3D"3337" data-end=3D"3354" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
337" data-end=3D"3354">Explication :</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"3355" data-end=3D"3766">
<li data-start=3D"3355" data-end=3D"3438" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3357" data-end=3D"3438" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
357" data-end=3D"3377"><code data-start=3D"3359" data-end=3D"3375">Buffered=
Reader</code></strong> : Cr=C3=A9e un tampon pour am=C3=A9liorer les perfor=
mances de lecture.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3439" data-end=3D"3495" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3441" data-end=3D"3495" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
441" data-end=3D"3457"><code data-start=3D"3443" data-end=3D"3455">FileRead=
er</code></strong> : Flux de lecture d'un fichier texte.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3496" data-end=3D"3621" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3498" data-end=3D"3621" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
498" data-end=3D"3514"><code data-start=3D"3500" data-end=3D"3512">readLine=
()</code></strong> : Permet de lire une ligne compl=C3=A8te =C3=A0 la fois.=
 Elle renvoie <code data-start=3D"3575" data-end=3D"3581">null</code> lorsq=
ue la fin du fichier est atteinte.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3622" data-end=3D"3766" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3624" data-end=3D"3766" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
624" data-end=3D"3648"><code data-start=3D"3626" data-end=3D"3646">try-with=
-resources</code></strong> : Cette syntaxe permet de s'assurer que le flux =
est ferm=C3=A9 automatiquement apr=C3=A8s utilisation, m=C3=AAme en cas d'e=
xception.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3768" data-end=3D"3815" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3772" data-end=3D"3815">2.3 Autres M=C3=A9thodes de <code data-start=3D"379=
7" data-end=3D"3813">BufferedReader</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3817" data-end=3D"3908" class=3D"">En plus de <code data-s=
tart=3D"3828" data-end=3D"3840">readLine()</code>, la classe <code data-sta=
rt=3D"3852" data-end=3D"3868">BufferedReader</code> offre d'autres m=C3=A9t=
hodes int=C3=A9ressantes :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3909" data-end=3D"4115">
<li data-start=3D"3909" data-end=3D"3958" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3911" data-end=3D"3958" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
911" data-end=3D"3923"><code data-start=3D"3913" data-end=3D"3921">read()</=
code></strong> : Lit un seul caract=C3=A8re =C3=A0 la fois.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3959" data-end=3D"4016" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3961" data-end=3D"4016" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
961" data-end=3D"3984"><code data-start=3D"3963" data-end=3D"3982">read(cha=
r[] cbuf)</code></strong> : Lit un tableau de caract=C3=A8res.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4017" data-end=3D"4070" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4019" data-end=3D"4070" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
019" data-end=3D"4037"><code data-start=3D"4021" data-end=3D"4035">skip(lon=
g n)</code></strong> : Ignore <code data-start=3D"4047" data-end=3D"4050">n=
</code> caract=C3=A8res du flux.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4071" data-end=3D"4115" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4073" data-end=3D"4115" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
073" data-end=3D"4086"><code data-start=3D"4075" data-end=3D"4084">close()<=
/code></strong> : Ferme le <code data-start=3D"4098" data-end=3D"4114">Buff=
eredReader</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4117" data-end=3D"4158" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4121" data-end=3D"4158">2.4 Avantages de <code data-start=3D"4140" data-end=
=3D"4156">BufferedReader</code></strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4160" data-end=3D"4473">
<li data-start=3D"4160" data-end=3D"4382" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4162" data-end=3D"4382" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
162" data-end=3D"4178">Performances</strong> : L'utilisation d'un buffer (m=
=C3=A9moire tampon) permet de r=C3=A9duire le nombre de lectures r=C3=A9ell=
es effectu=C3=A9es sur le disque, ce qui am=C3=A9liore les performances, su=
rtout lors de la lecture de fichiers volumineux.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4383" data-end=3D"4473" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4385" data-end=3D"4473" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
385" data-end=3D"4406">Lecture par ligne</strong> : Il permet une lecture s=
imple ligne par ligne des fichiers texte.</p>
</li>
</ul>
