<h2 data-start=3D"6569" data-end=3D"6588" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6572" data-end=3D"6586">Conclusion</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"6590" data-end=3D"6772" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"6593" data-end=3D"6634">Single Responsibility Principle (SRP)</strong> =
est un <strong data-start=3D"6642" data-end=3D"6658">principe cl=C3=A9</str=
ong> en programmation orient=C3=A9e objet qui permet d=E2=80=99am=C3=A9lior=
er la lisibilit=C3=A9, la maintenance et la testabilit=C3=A9 du code.</p>
<p data-start=3D"6774" data-end=3D"6995" class=3D"">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-=
start=3D"6776" data-end=3D"6829">Chaque classe doit avoir une seule respons=
abilit=C3=A9</strong>.<br data-start=3D"6830" data-end=3D"6833">
=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"6835" data-end=3D"6914">Diviser les classes=
 en unit=C3=A9s logiques pour =C3=A9viter les d=C3=A9pendances inutiles</st=
rong>.<br data-start=3D"6915" data-end=3D"6918">
=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"6920" data-end=3D"6992">Utiliser le SRP ave=
c mod=C3=A9ration pour =C3=A9viter une explosion de classes</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"6997" data-end=3D"7105" class=3D"">En appliquant ce princi=
