<h2 data-start=3D"64" data-end=3D"85" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"67" =
data-end=3D"83">Introduction</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"87" data-end=3D"296" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=3D"9=
0" data-end=3D"129">Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP)</strong> est le tro=
isi=C3=A8me principe du <strong data-start=3D"159" data-end=3D"168">SOLID</=
strong> en programmation orient=C3=A9e objet. Il a =C3=A9t=C3=A9 formul=C3=
=A9 par Barbara Liskov en 1987 et d=C3=A9finit une r=C3=A8gle fondamentale =
pour l=E2=80=99h=C3=A9ritage.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"298" data-end=3D"325" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"30=
2" data-end=3D"323">D=C3=A9finition du LSP</strong></h3>
<blockquote data-start=3D"326" data-end=3D"485">
<p data-start=3D"328" data-end=3D"485" class=3D""><em data-start=3D"328" da=
ta-end=3D"485">Si S est une sous-classe de T, alors les objets de type T pe=
uvent =C3=AAtre remplac=C3=A9s par des objets de type S sans modifier le bo=
n fonctionnement du programme.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"487" data-end=3D"606" class=3D"">En d=E2=80=99autres terme=
s, une sous-classe doit pouvoir <strong data-start=3D"536" data-end=3D"549"=
>remplacer</strong> sa classe m=C3=A8re <strong data-start=3D"565" data-end=
=3D"605">sans alt=C3=A9rer le comportement attendu</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"608" data-end=3D"639" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"61=
2" data-end=3D"637">Objectifs du tutoriel</strong></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"640" data-end=3D"890">
<li data-start=3D"640" data-end=3D"680" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"643" data-end=3D"680" class=3D"">Comprendre <strong data-s=
tart=3D"654" data-end=3D"677">l'importance du LSP</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"681" data-end=3D"721" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"684" data-end=3D"721" class=3D"">D=C3=A9tecter <strong dat=
a-start=3D"693" data-end=3D"718">les violations du LSP</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"722" data-end=3D"774" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"725" data-end=3D"774" class=3D"">Apprendre <strong data-st=
art=3D"735" data-end=3D"763">comment appliquer le LSP</strong> en Java.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"775" data-end=3D"834" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"778" data-end=3D"834" class=3D"">=C3=89tudier <strong data=
