<h2 data-start=3D"897" data-end=3D"962" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"90=
0" data-end=3D"960">1. Pourquoi appliquer le Liskov Substitution Principle =
?</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"964" data-end=3D"1355" class=3D"">=E2=9C=94 <strong data-s=
tart=3D"966" data-end=3D"988">Code plus coh=C3=A9rent</strong> : Une classe=
 d=C3=A9riv=C3=A9e doit <strong data-start=3D"1015" data-end=3D"1044">pr=C3=
=A9server le comportement</strong> de la classe m=C3=A8re.<br data-start=3D=
"1063" data-end=3D"1066">
=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"1068" data-end=3D"1095">Facilit=C3=A9 de ma=
intenance</strong> : On peut utiliser la sous-classe sans surprise ni r=C3=
=A9gression.<br data-start=3D"1158" data-end=3D"1161">
=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"1163" data-end=3D"1185">R=C3=A9duction des =
bugs</strong> : Pas de comportements inattendus li=C3=A9s =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99=
h=C3=A9ritage.<br data-start=3D"1238" data-end=3D"1241">
=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"1243" data-end=3D"1271">Respect du polymorp=
hisme</strong> : Permet une utilisation fluide des objets de sous-classes d=
ans le code existant.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1357" data-end=3D"1360" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1362" data-end=3D"1416" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1365" data-end=3D"1414">2. Violation du Liskov Substitution Principle</stro=
ng></h2>
<p data-start=3D"1418" data-end=3D"1585" class=3D"">Une violation du LSP se=
