=C3=A9narios o=C3=B9 il est n=C3=A9cessaire de <strong data-start=3D"209" d=
ata-end=3D"243">mettre =C3=A0 jour plusieurs objets</strong> en r=C3=A9pons=
e =C3=A0 des changements dans un autre objet. C=E2=80=99est un des <strong =
data-start=3D"307" data-end=3D"334">patrons comportementaux</strong>, ce qu=
i signifie qu=E2=80=99il se concentre sur la mani=C3=A8re dont les objets i=
nteragissent entre eux.</p>
<p data-start=3D"428" data-end=3D"634" class=3D"">Dans ce tutoriel, nous al=
lons explorer le <strong data-start=3D"470" data-end=3D"490">pattern Observ=
er</strong> en d=C3=A9tail, de la d=C3=A9finition aux impl=C3=A9mentations =
pratiques en Java, en passant par les avantages, les inconv=C3=A9nients et =
les meilleures pratiques.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"636" data-end=3D"639" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"641" data-end=3D"693" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"64=
4" data-end=3D"693">1. Qu'est-ce que le Design Pattern Observer ?</strong><=
/h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"695" data-end=3D"713" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"69=
9" data-end=3D"713">D=C3=A9finition</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"714" data-end=3D"1028" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=3D=
"717" data-end=3D"737">Observer Pattern</strong> d=C3=A9finit une relation =
<strong data-start=3D"759" data-end=3D"777">un-=C3=A0-plusieurs</strong> en=
tre objets. Un objet appel=C3=A9 <strong data-start=3D"808" data-end=3D"827=
">sujet (subject)</strong> est surveill=C3=A9 par plusieurs objets appel=C3=
=A9s <strong data-start=3D"871" data-end=3D"899">observateurs (observers)</=
strong>. D=C3=A8s qu'un changement se produit dans l'=C3=A9tat du sujet, <s=
trong data-start=3D"955" data-end=3D"980">tous les observateurs</strong> so=
nt inform=C3=A9s et peuvent r=C3=A9agir en cons=C3=A9quence.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1030" data-end=3D"1041" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1034" data-end=3D"1041">But</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1042" data-end=3D"1210">
<li data-start=3D"1042" data-end=3D"1121" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1044" data-end=3D"1121" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
044" data-end=3D"1073">Informer plusieurs objets</strong> d'un changement d=
'=C3=A9tat sans trop de d=C3=A9pendance.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1122" data-end=3D"1207" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1124" data-end=3D"1207" class=3D"">D=C3=A9-coupler la logi=
que entre l'objet qui <strong data-start=3D"1164" data-end=3D"1175">notifie=
</strong> et les objets qui <strong data-start=3D"1194" data-end=3D"1206">=
=C3=A9coutent</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1211" data-end=3D"1236" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1215" data-end=3D"1236">Exemple classique</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1237" data-end=3D"1438" class=3D"">Un exemple classique de=
 ce pattern est celui des <strong data-start=3D"1286" data-end=3D"1314">abo=
nn=C3=A9s =C3=A0 une newsletter</strong>. L=E2=80=99=C3=A9diteur du site (l=
e sujet) envoie une mise =C3=A0 jour aux abonn=C3=A9s (les observateurs) d=
=C3=A8s qu=E2=80=99il y a une nouvelle publication.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1440" data-end=3D"1443" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1445" data-end=3D"1493" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1448" data-end=3D"1493">2. Pourquoi utiliser l'Observer Pattern ?</strong><=
/h2>
<p data-start=3D"1495" data-end=3D"1558" class=3D"">Voici quelques raisons =
de choisir ce pattern dans vos projets :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1560" data-end=3D"1850">
<li data-start=3D"1560" data-end=3D"1666" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1562" data-end=3D"1666" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
562" data-end=3D"1576">D=C3=A9couplage</strong> : Le sujet et ses observate=
urs sont faiblement coupl=C3=A9s, ce qui facilite leur maintenance.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1667" data-end=3D"1757" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1669" data-end=3D"1757" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
669" data-end=3D"1683">R=C3=A9activit=C3=A9</strong> : Plusieurs objets peu=
vent r=C3=A9agir en m=C3=AAme temps au changement d'un objet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1758" data-end=3D"1850" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1760" data-end=3D"1850" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
760" data-end=3D"1775">Flexibilit=C3=A9</strong> : Il est facile d'ajouter =
de nouveaux observateurs sans modifier le sujet.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1852" data-end=3D"1855" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1857" data-end=3D"1911" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1860" data-end=3D"1911">3. Impl=C3=A9mentation de l'Observer Pattern en Jav=
a</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1913" data-end=3D"1943" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1917" data-end=3D"1943">3.1. Structure de base</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1945" data-end=3D"2004" class=3D"">Le mod=C3=A8le Observer=
 est compos=C3=A9 de plusieurs =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments cl=C3=A9s :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2006" data-end=3D"2394">
<li data-start=3D"2006" data-end=3D"2104" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2008" data-end=3D"2104" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
008" data-end=3D"2027">Subject (Sujet)</strong> : L'objet qui maintient une=
 liste d'observateurs et notifie les changements.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2105" data-end=3D"2182" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2107" data-end=3D"2182" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
107" data-end=3D"2133">Observer (Observateur)</strong> : L'objet qui attend=
 les notifications du sujet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2183" data-end=3D"2283" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2185" data-end=3D"2283" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
185" data-end=3D"2220">ConcreteSubject (Sujet concret)</strong> : L'impl=C3=
=A9mentation du sujet qui maintient l'=C3=A9tat =C3=A0 surveiller.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2284" data-end=3D"2394" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2286" data-end=3D"2394" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
286" data-end=3D"2328">ConcreteObserver (Observateur concret)</strong> : L'=
impl=C3=A9mentation d'un observateur qui r=C3=A9agit aux notifications.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"2396" data-end=3D"2445" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2400" data-end=3D"2445">3.2. Code d'exemple pour Observer Pattern</strong><=
/h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"2447" data-end=3D"2494" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2452" data-end=3D"2494">1=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Cr=C3=A9ation de l'interface <c=
ode data-start=3D"2482" data-end=3D"2492">Observer</code></strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"2496" data-end=3D"2597" class=3D"">L'interface <code data-=
start=3D"2508" data-end=3D"2518">Observer</code> d=C3=A9finit une m=C3=A9th=
ode <code data-start=3D"2539" data-end=3D"2549">update()</code> qui sera ap=
pel=C3=A9e pour notifier les changements.</p>
<pre class=3D"!overflow-visible" data-start=3D"2599" data-end=3D"2666"><div=
 class=3D"contain-inline-size rounded-md border-[0.5px] border-token-border=
-medium relative bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary"><div class=3D"flex items=
-center text-token-text-secondary px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans justify-betwe=
en h-9 bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary dark:bg-token-main-surface-secondar=
y select-none rounded-t-[5px]">java</div><div class=3D"sticky top-9"><div c=
lass=3D"absolute bottom-0 right-0 flex h-9 items-center pr-2"><div class=3D=
