<h3 data-start=3D"4954" data-end=3D"5000" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4958" data-end=3D"5000">5.1. Un Test Unitaire Par Comportement</strong></h3=
>
<p data-start=3D"5002" data-end=3D"5186" class=3D"">Chaque test doit =C3=AA=
tre con=C3=A7u pour tester une <strong data-start=3D"5046" data-end=3D"5082=
">unit=C3=A9 sp=C3=A9cifique de comportement</strong>. Si un test couvre tr=
op de fonctionnalit=C3=A9s =C3=A0 la fois, il devient difficile =C3=A0 comp=
rendre et =C3=A0 maintenir.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"5188" data-end=3D"5232" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5192" data-end=3D"5232">5.2. Utiliser des Assertions Claires</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5234" data-end=3D"5346" class=3D"">Utilisez des assertions=
 claires pour v=C3=A9rifier les r=C3=A9sultats attendus. Quelques exemples =
d'assertions courantes :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5348" data-end=3D"5484">
<li data-start=3D"5348" data-end=3D"5382" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5350" data-end=3D"5382" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"535=
0" data-end=3D"5382">assertEquals(expected, actual)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5383" data-end=3D"5408" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5385" data-end=3D"5408" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"538=
5" data-end=3D"5408">assertTrue(condition)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5409" data-end=3D"5435" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5411" data-end=3D"5435" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"541=
1" data-end=3D"5435">assertFalse(condition)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5436" data-end=3D"5458" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5438" data-end=3D"5458" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"543=
8" data-end=3D"5458">assertNull(object)</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5459" data-end=3D"5484" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5461" data-end=3D"5484" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"546=
1" data-end=3D"5484">assertNotNull(object)</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5486" data-end=3D"5545" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5490" data-end=3D"5545">5.3. Organiser les Tests avec <code data-start=3D"5=
522" data-end=3D"5531">@Before</code> et <code data-start=3D"5535" data-end=
=3D"5543">@After</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5547" data-end=3D"5772" class=3D"">Utilisez les annotation=
s <code data-start=3D"5572" data-end=3D"5581">@Before</code> et <code data-=
start=3D"5585" data-end=3D"5593">@After</code> pour effectuer des op=C3=A9r=
ations avant et apr=C3=A8s chaque test. Par exemple, vous pouvez initialise=
r des objets co=C3=BBteux =C3=A0 cr=C3=A9er dans <code data-start=3D"5721" =
data-end=3D"5730">@Before</code> et nettoyer les ressources dans <code data=
-start=3D"5763" data-end=3D"5771">@After</code>.</p>
