ode></strong> : La m=C3=A9thode <code data-start=3D"3843" data-end=3D"3859"=
>testAddition()</code> est marqu=C3=A9e comme un test unitaire, et JUnit l'=
ex=C3=A9cutera comme un test.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3932" data-end=3D"4092" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3934" data-end=3D"4092" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
934" data-end=3D"3970"><code data-start=3D"3936" data-end=3D"3968">assertEq=
uals(expected, actual)</code></strong> : Cette m=C3=A9thode est utilis=C3=
=A9e pour v=C3=A9rifier que la valeur retourn=C3=A9e par la m=C3=A9thode te=
st=C3=A9e correspond =C3=A0 la valeur attendue.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4094" data-end=3D"4097" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4099" data-end=3D"4136" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4102" data-end=3D"4136">3. Assertions et V=C3=A9rifications</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"4138" data-end=3D"4368" class=3D"">Les assertions sont uti=
lis=C3=A9es pour v=C3=A9rifier que les r=C3=A9sultats obtenus correspondent=
 =C3=A0 ce qui est attendu. JUnit fournit plusieurs m=C3=A9thodes d'asserti=
on, qui peuvent =C3=AAtre utilis=C3=A9es pour effectuer des tests sur les v=
aleurs attendues.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4370" data-end=3D"4408" class=3D"">3.1. Assertions les pl=
us courantes</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4410" data-end=3D"4947">
<li data-start=3D"4410" data-end=3D"4492" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4412" data-end=3D"4492" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
412" data-end=3D"4448"><code data-start=3D"4414" data-end=3D"4446">assertEq=
uals(expected, actual)</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que les deux valeurs =
sont =C3=A9gales.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4493" data-end=3D"4585" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4495" data-end=3D"4585" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
495" data-end=3D"4534"><code data-start=3D"4497" data-end=3D"4532">assertNo=
tEquals(expected, actual)</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que les deux valeu=
rs ne sont pas =C3=A9gales.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4586" data-end=3D"4653" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4588" data-end=3D"4653" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
588" data-end=3D"4615"><code data-start=3D"4590" data-end=3D"4613">assertTr=
ue(condition)</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que la condition est vraie.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4654" data-end=3D"4723" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4656" data-end=3D"4723" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
656" data-end=3D"4684"><code data-start=3D"4658" data-end=3D"4682">assertFa=
lse(condition)</code></strong> : V=C3=A9rifie que la condition est fausse.<=
/p>
</li>
