<li data-start=3D"4335" data-end=3D"4448" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4337" data-end=3D"4448" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
337" data-end=3D"4348"><code data-start=3D"4339" data-end=3D"4346">build</c=
ode></strong> : Les informations de configuration li=C3=A9es =C3=A0 la cons=
truction du projet (compilateur, plugins, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4450" data-end=3D"4479" class=3D"">1.5. Utilisation de Ma=
ven</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4481" data-end=3D"4676" class=3D"">Pour utiliser Maven, vo=
us devez avoir <strong data-start=3D"4519" data-end=3D"4527">Java</strong> =
et <strong data-start=3D"4531" data-end=3D"4540">Maven</strong> install=C3=
=A9s sur votre machine. Ensuite, vous pouvez ex=C3=A9cuter des commandes de=
puis la ligne de commande pour accomplir diff=C3=A9rentes t=C3=A2ches.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4678" data-end=3D"4714" class=3D"">Quelques commandes Mave=
n courantes :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4716" data-end=3D"5032">
<li data-start=3D"4716" data-end=3D"4798" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4718" data-end=3D"4798" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
718" data-end=3D"4733"><code data-start=3D"4720" data-end=3D"4731">mvn clea=
n</code></strong> : Supprime les fichiers g=C3=A9n=C3=A9r=C3=A9s lors de la=
 derni=C3=A8re compilation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4799" data-end=3D"4844" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4801" data-end=3D"4844" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
801" data-end=3D"4818"><code data-start=3D"4803" data-end=3D"4816">mvn comp=
ile</code></strong> : Compile le code source.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4845" data-end=3D"4892" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4847" data-end=3D"4892" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
847" data-end=3D"4861"><code data-start=3D"4849" data-end=3D"4859">mvn test=
</code></strong> : Ex=C3=A9cute les tests unitaires.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4893" data-end=3D"4969" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4895" data-end=3D"4969" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
895" data-end=3D"4912"><code data-start=3D"4897" data-end=3D"4910">mvn pack=
age</code></strong> : Cr=C3=A9e un artefact (par exemple, un fichier JAR ou=
 WAR).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4970" data-end=3D"5032" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4972" data-end=3D"5032" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
972" data-end=3D"4989"><code data-start=3D"4974" data-end=3D"4987">mvn inst=
all</code></strong> : Installe l'artefact dans le d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t local.</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5034" data-end=3D"5037" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5039" data-end=3D"5071" class=3D"">2. <strong data-start=
=3D"5045" data-end=3D"5071">Qu'est-ce que Gradle ?</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5073" data-end=3D"5104" class=3D"">2.1. Pr=C3=A9sentation=
 de Gradle</h3>
<p data-start=3D"5106" data-end=3D"5590" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
106" data-end=3D"5116">Gradle</strong> est un outil de gestion de projet et=
 d'automatisation de construction open-source qui a gagn=C3=A9 en popularit=
=C3=A9 pour sa flexibilit=C3=A9 et ses performances. Contrairement =C3=A0 M=
aven, qui est bas=C3=A9 sur XML, Gradle utilise un DSL (Domain Specific Lan=
guage) bas=C3=A9 sur <strong data-start=3D"5369" data-end=3D"5379">Groovy</=
strong> (ou Kotlin, pour Gradle Kotlin DSL) pour configurer les projets. Gr=
adle est con=C3=A7u pour =C3=AAtre rapide, flexible et hautement personnali=
sable, ce qui en fait un excellent choix pour les projets de grande envergu=
re.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"5592" data-end=3D"5627" class=3D"">2.2. Pourquoi utiliser=
 Gradle ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"5629" data-end=3D"5684" class=3D"">Les raisons pour lesque=
lles Gradle est populaire sont :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5685" data-end=3D"6251">
<li data-start=3D"5685" data-end=3D"5854" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5687" data-end=3D"5854" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
687" data-end=3D"5712">Performance am=C3=A9lior=C3=A9e</strong> : Gr=C3=A2c=
e =C3=A0 des optimisations comme le cache local et l'ex=C3=A9cution incr=C3=
=A9mentielle, Gradle peut construire des projets plus rapidement que Maven.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5855" data-end=3D"5986" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5857" data-end=3D"5986" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
857" data-end=3D"5872">Flexibilit=C3=A9</strong> : Le langage de script Gro=
ovy permet une grande personnalisation et la possibilit=C3=A9 d'=C3=A9crire=
 des t=C3=A2ches complexes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5987" data-end=3D"6098" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5989" data-end=3D"6098" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
989" data-end=3D"6020">Interop=C3=A9rabilit=C3=A9 avec Maven</strong> : Gra=
dle peut facilement utiliser des biblioth=C3=A8ques et des d=C3=A9pendances=
 Maven.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6099" data-end=3D"6251" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6101" data-end=3D"6251" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
101" data-end=3D"6128">Gestion des d=C3=A9pendances</strong> : Gradle g=C3=
=A8re aussi bien les d=C3=A9pendances Maven que les d=C3=A9pendances locale=
s ou d'autres syst=C3=A8mes de gestion de d=C3=A9pendances.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6253" data-end=3D"6290" class=3D"">2.3. Structure d'un pr=
ojet Gradle</h3>
<p data-start=3D"6292" data-end=3D"6393" class=3D"">Un projet Gradle suit u=
ne structure diff=C3=A9rente de celle de Maven, mais les concepts sont simi=
